    "done_when": "Per the plan's section 4 and decision wall-from-coil-vv-tables. (1) Copy /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/jtmm-geometry-source/copies/jt-60sa/.local/share/machine_description/coil_geometry/coil_vv_OP1.dat into /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/source/coil_vv_OP1.dat, refusing unless its sha256 is 55d97f6989368348108aef384b1ff1b737803fa9be6ac0b84aa718bedfda01cb (the jtmm-geometry-source inventory), and add it to /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/source/provenance.json beside the other three copies. (2) imas_ambix/data/selene_deck.py builds the wall for each phase from that phase's coil_vv deck. The limiter unit (wall/description_2d/limiter/unit/outline) is the nlim=51 first-wall polygon (OP1 line 393, OP2 line 371). One vessel unit's annular outline_inner and outline_outer are the 128-row contour block's 'Inner VV=50' and 'Outer VV=50' polylines, excluding its 28 D-probe rows. pf_passive keeps the vessel from each phase's deck and the CRYOSTAT loop from EQSLE.DATA, as now. The cryostat group is accepted only if every one of its filaments lies outside the vessel's outer-skin polyline, a containment test replacing the bounding-box test. Tests in tests/data/test_selene_deck.py assert, for both phases: a limiter of 51 points that is a closed contour; inner and outer outlines of 51 points each; no D-probe point in either; and the OP1 and OP2 limiters differing. (3) Re-convert OP1 and OP2 from the sha256-verified copies (refuse on any mismatch with provenance.json). Record every existing file's sha256 first, write each new file under a temporary name and rename it into place (a peer session's figures read this store), remove the staging directory afterwards including the empty /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/.convert-1165829 left by the previous run, and read every file back through imas.DBEntry at DD 4.1.1. (4) imas_ambix/data/machine_maps/jt-60sa.json binds the limiter and ves